A TEST BUILD: WHAT IS ALLOWED

Builds are published openly, on the releases page
https://github.com/ValentinArtas/automaton-release/releases — so that they can
be taken and tried. Anyone who downloads a build from there is thereby given
permission to install it and use it on their own computers for their own
purposes, free of charge and with no time limit.

The permission covers the build, not the source: the source code is not
published and stays closed. That is deliberate, not an oversight.

The permission is personal: it does not travel with a copy to anybody else.
The prohibitions above remain in force — in particular, you may not host the
build yourself, sell it, or use it to provide services to others. To pass the
program to somebody, give them the link to the releases page, so that they
receive the permission the same way you did.

This is a **test version**, a release below 1.0. It may change, it may hold
mistakes, and workflows built in it may need fixing after an update. Remarks
and mistakes you find are welcome at
https://github.com/ValentinArtas/automaton-release/issues — that helps, but it
obliges you to nothing.

The copyright holder may change the terms for future releases. For the build
you have already downloaded, the permission stays as it is.

The program is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. The copyright
holder is not liable for any damages arising from its use, including loss of
data and the consequences of automations you have set up yourself.

The program contains code by other authors under their own terms, listed in
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md. Those terms remain in force; this file neither
overrides them nor could.

